 the league. [[p:7564|Ja'Marr Chase]] led the club with 358.20 points in 15 starts, followed by [[p:5849|Kyler Murray]] (253.32). The season high was 176.98 in week 10 ([[g:2024-10-4-12]]). In the Toilet Bowl they beat [[f:4|Win one game]] 118.78-92.90 in the Toilet Bowl First Round, then lost to [[f:3|Kolkata Kommies]] 123.30-152.28 in the Seventh Place Game and finished 8th. The front office made 10 transactions, 3 of them trades. [[p:7564|Ja'Marr Chase]] was the league MVP. Young Sexy Award winners on the roster at season's end: Brian Thomas (WR). [[m:dan]] acquired a stake on 2024-10-22."},{"season":"2025","heading":"2025: Happy Feet","text":"Under Colin and Dan, Happy Feet went 3-11 to finish as the No. 12 seed, scoring 1249.27 points, 12th in the league. [[p:4892|Baker Mayfield]] led the club with 239.52 points in 15 starts, followed by [[p:7564|Ja'Marr Chase]] (195.20). The season high was 123.48 in week 3 ([[g:2025-03-10-12]]). In the Toilet Bowl they lost to [[f:11|BubbaNASTIES]] 54.60-133.68 in the Toilet Bowl Semifinal, then lost to [[f:2|Storm FC]] 44.94-113.08 in the Toilet Bowl Final and were crowned Ultimate Loser. The front office made 11 transactions, 3 of them trades."},{"season":"2026","heading":"2026: Team Win One Game","text":"Through 4 games under Charlie, Team Win One Game are 1-3 and 12th in the standings, with 440.74 points (12th). [[p:6786|CeeDee Lamb]] led the club with 71.00 points in 3 starts, followed by [[p:12481|Cam Skattebo]] (51.00). The season high was 128.00 in week 4 ([[g:2026-04-2-12]]). The front office made 31 transactions, 3 of them trades. The club was renamed 3 times during the year, ending as Team Win One Game. [[m:colin]] gave up his stake on 2026-01-05. [[m:dan]] gave up his stake on 2026-01-05. [[m:charlie]] acquired a stake on 2026-01-05."}],"moves":[{"season":"2023","trades":4,"claims":1,"signings":0,"adds":1,"releases":0,"gs":44,"pts":714.9},{"season":"2024","trades":3,"claims":0,"signings":2,"adds":2,"releases":7,"g